Definitely

> - On final run use cursed !GL as much as possible, and save some for the
> no-teleport levels.  

> I used three wand wishes for a total of 5 c!GL

They aren't THAT important.  Many of the no-tele levels can be traversed in 
about 20 turns, depending on stair placement.

Do note that you can alchemize !oGL.  This is where polypiling comes in handy, 
because it gives you both more alchemy fodder and more !oGL.  

> Digging down in Gehennom will save time, esp. if you'll be using c!GL to 
> come back up.

Digging down is good everywhere.  Your goal pre-castle should be to accumulate 
as much Stuff, including polyfodder, in as few turns as possible.  That means 
skipping levels that don't have much Stuff. 
 
> NO STASHES!!! Avoid backtracking, don't collect junk.

I like to make a stash in Sokoban and travel there with the Eye.  Also I make 
a temporary stash Minesend and another in Minetown.  Later on in the game I'll 
gate back to Minesend, climb up to Minetown and finish the level, then grab my 
stash there and gate to Sokoban.

> Probably the best thing you could do (in terms of sheer turn count): 
